      "side": 1,
      "message": "**The \"Related Header\" Include Order (`util/focaltech/ft_scsi.cc` \u0026 `usb_context.cc`)** You have comments in your implementation files saying:\n\n```c\n// To prevent the formatter from rearranging the header include order.\n#include \"ft_scsi.h\"\n\n```\n\n* **The Issue:** The Google C++ Style Guide explicitly mandates that a `.cc` file\u0027s *first* include must be its related `.h` file (e.g., `ft_scsi.cc` must include `ft_scsi.h` before `\u003cbit\u003e`, `\u003cendian.h\u003e`, or anything else). This rule exists to ensure that every header is completely self-contained and doesn\u0027t secretly rely on includes from the `.cc` file.  \n* **Remediation:** Remove the comment and move `#include \"ft_scsi.h\"` to the very top of `ft_scsi.cc`. Do the same for `usb_context.h` in `usb_context.cc`. Let `clang-format` do its job; it is trying to enforce the correct Google style rule.",
